            "strategy": "Category C — Work Elimination. Root cause: the iter_0 code allocated 4 arrays indexed by max_orderkey (~60M), totaling ~1GB of zero-initialized memory, but only ~3.5M entries were used. This allocation+initialization dominated runtime (593ms total vs ~55ms in measured phases). Fix: replace all max_orderkey-sized arrays with compact arrays sized to the number of qualifying orders (~3.5M). Store (orderkey, orderdate, shippriority, revenue) in a single compact struct array. Sort qualifying orderkeys before lineitem probe for sequential access. Fuse aggregation into the probe loop — since each orderkey is unique among qualifying orders, accumulate revenue directly into the compact array slot. This reduces memory from ~1GB to ~56MB and eliminates the initialization bottleneck.",
