            "validation": "pass",
            "strategy": "Category B+C — Algorithm change + Work elimination. Three root causes: (1) MAP_POPULATE pre-faults page tables for ~706MB (including the 458MB lineitem index where only 6% of entries are accessed), costing 33ms — fix: disable MAP_POPULATE for all files, use demand-paging. (2) Lineitem data columns use MADV_RANDOM which disables OS prefetching, yet access is sequential (sorted qualifying orderkeys) — this causes ~200K unnecessary soft page faults, explaining the 36ms unaccounted time in iter_1. Fix: use MADV_SEQUENTIAL for lineitem data columns, MADV_SEQUENTIAL for orders columns, MADV_RANDOM only for the lineitem index. (3) The merge_sort phase copies 84MB from per-thread vectors to a single array (22ms). Fix: two-pass approach — count qualifying rows per thread in pass 1, compute prefix sums, write directly to pre-allocated shared array in pass 2. Additional: late materialize o_shippriority (skip scanning 60MB, only load for top-10 results). Use schedule(static) for lineitem probe to maintain sequential access. Expected savings: data_loading 33ms→~2ms, unaccounted 36ms→~5ms, merge 22ms→0ms, scan 18ms→~14ms.",
